From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:32:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] keytable: always inline emitBit() of the manchester decoder

clang 23 no longer inlines emitBit(), a static function without the
inline keyword: it keeps it as a BPF subprogram in .text and calls it
from the program, with a relocation on the call instruction.
ir-keytable's loader (bpf_load.c) loads only the program section and
patches only ld_imm64 instructions, so the decoder is refused
("invalid relo for insn[222].code 0x85") and manchester remotes stop
working. Older clang inlined the function, as in the objects LibreELEC
precompiled from v4l-utils 1.22.0 in 2021, whose single program makes
no call.

Force the inlining, which gives the loader the single program it
expects. The other eight decoders only use static inline helpers and
compile to a single program as they are.
---
 utils/keytable/bpf_protocols/manchester.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/utils/keytable/bpf_protocols/manchester.c b/utils/keytable/bpf_protocols/manchester.c
index 0310f37e9ab5..c34b03d07995 100644
--- a/utils/keytable/bpf_protocols/manchester.c
+++ b/utils/keytable/bpf_protocols/manchester.c
@@ -55,7 +55,8 @@ static inline int eq_margin(unsigned d1, unsigned d2)
 #define STATE_MID0     4
 #define STATE_START0   5
 
-static int emitBit(unsigned int *sample, struct decoder_state *s, int bit, int state)
+static inline __attribute__((always_inline))
+int emitBit(unsigned int *sample, struct decoder_state *s, int bit, int state)
 {
 	s->bits <<= 1;
 	s->bits |= bit;
